\section{Formatting the run header}

The run header is a plain-text block with key--value fields.
We keep it simple---no YAML, no JSON---so it is easy to read in
[[git log]] output.

The [[Run-Id:]] field is what a reader matches against the trailer
commit.
It is optional because reconstructed histories (\cref{progsnap2}) build
complete blocks that need no partner commit to look for.

<<functions>>=
def format_run_header(script, args, start_time,
                      run_id=None):
    """Format a run header block.

    The header records which script was run, its arguments, and
    the start time.  When ``run_id`` is given, it is recorded as
    the ``Run-Id`` field that links this run to its trailer.
    """
    args_str = " ".join(args) if args else "(none)"
    lines = [
        f"Run: {script} {args_str}",
        "",
        f"Script: {script}",
        f"Arguments: {args_str}",
        f"Start-Time: {start_time.isoformat()}",
    ]
    if run_id:
        lines.append(f"{RUN_ID_FIELD} {run_id}")
    return "\n".join(lines)
<<constants>>=
RUN_ID_FIELD = "Run-Id:"
@

